    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the `AUDIT` logger call after a successful owner save) now also logs `membershipNumber` alongside the fields it already emitted (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`).\n\n**Change made** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:539`):\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n    ownerMapper.formatMembershipLevel(owner), ownerMapper.formatMembershipNumber(owner));\n```\n\nI reused the existing `ownerMapper.formatMembershipNumber(owner)` \u2014 the same formatter used to populate the DTO's `membershipNumber` \u2014 so the audited value matches what the API returns (e.g. `NSW-16E6609E-M26`).\n\n**Test results:**\n- New `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes.\n- Full suite: **262 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
